    "final_answer": "I have the complete data for the America East Conference standings. Let me analyze it carefully:\n\n**America East Conference Standings (2025-26 Season):**\n\n| Team | Conference W-L | Overall W-L |\n|------|---------------|-------------|\n| UMBC Retrievers | 14-2 | 24-9 |\n| Vermont Catamounts | 12-4 | 22-12 |\n| NJIT Highlanders | 10-6 | 16-17 |\n| UMass Lowell River Hawks | 9-7 | 15-18 |\n| UAlbany Great Danes | 7-9 | 11-21 |\n| Maine Black Bears | 6-10 | 8-24 |\n| New Hampshire Wildcats | 5-11 | 9-21 |\n| Bryant Bulldogs | 5-11 | 9-22 |\n| Binghamton Bearcats | 4-12 | 8-23 |\n\n## Answer\n\n**No teams in the America East Conference currently have equal wins and losses** (neither in Conference play nor in Overall record).\n\nLooking at every team:\n- **Conference records**: 14-2, 12-4, 10-6, 9-7, 7-9, 6-10, 5-11, 5-11, 4-12 — none are equal\n- **Overall records**: 24-9, 22-12, 16-17, 15-18, 11-21, 8-24, 9-21, 9-22, 8-23 — none are equal\n\nThe closest matches are:\n- **New Hampshire Wildcats** and **Bryant Bulldogs** both have an identical **5-11 Conference record** (same wins and same losses, though not equal within their own record)\n- **UAlbany Great Danes** and **NJIT Highlanders** also have win-loss splits close to mirror images (UAlbany: 7-9 conf / 11-21 overall; NJIT: 10-6 conf / 16-17 overall)\n\nBut strictly speaking, **no team in the America East Conference has equal wins and losses** in either their Conference or Overall standings.",
